  "label": "User projected onto the confused bulldog scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual scene of the confused bulldog, as the meme uses the dog's expression as a metaphor for human confusion. The user identifies with the experience of confusion, projecting their own emotional state onto the bulldog's face. This projection is implicit, not explicit (e.g., no 'me' or 'you' text), but is strongly implied by the anthropomorphism and the relatable nature of the humor. The user sees themselves in the dog's bewildered state, making the bulldog the visual anchor for their own experience.",
